oubleshooting row\n- [ ] 7.2 `docs/scaling.md`: record that every process holding an MCP catalog — including `web`-profile API processes — runs one child process per configured stdio server\n- [ ] 7.3 `SPEC.md` §99: replace \"stdio do not ship\" with the shipped two-transport statement\n- [ ] 7.4 `VISION.md:156`: remove local stdio MCP processes from the deliberate deferrals\n- [ ] 7.5 `apps/api/AGENTS.md`: extend the Remote MCP tools section with the stdio entry shape, the explicit-environment rule, and the retry difference from HTTP\n- [ ] 7.6 `README.md`: document the stdio entry alongside the remote one and soften \"`.mcp.json`-compatible\" to \"`.mcp.json`-shaped\"\n- [ ] 7.7 `CHANGELOG.md`: add the dated entry\n- [ ] 7.8 `apps/api/llame.config.json.example`: add a commented stdio entry\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- [ ] 8.1 `pnpm --filter api test` and `pnpm --filter api test:integration` pass\n- [ ] 8.2 `pnpm --filter api lint`, `pnpm --filter api typecheck`, and `pnpm format:check` pass\n- [ ] 8.3 `pnpm test:e2e -- e2e/web/chat/mcp-tool.spec.ts` passes for both transports\n- [ ] 8.4 Manually verify one real stdio server end to end — configure it, allowlist one read-only tool, execute it in a chat, confirm history replay, and confirm no declared secret appears in logs, run events, or the receipt\n- [ ] 8.5 `openspec validate add-stdio-mcp-servers --strict` passes\n",
